The Competitor library brings creative records, advertiser matching and source details into the same review. Collected ads can be checked, verified or discarded before they support a brief. The output can then inform original hooks, creative angles and test ideas.

For marketing work, that distinction matters: seeing an ad in a public library tells me what a competitor is running. It does not tell me their CPA, ROAS or whether the creative is profitable. I use the evidence to develop a testable direction, then judge it against our own results.
